  "text": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
    "text": "<p>Stryker is aware of the SweynTooth Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) vulnerabilities and is closely monitoring and assessing the situation. Our product security team has taken precautions to secure our products from these new vulnerabilities. To date, we have not received any reports of this vulnerability impacting our devices.</p>\n<p>A thorough evaluation of all potentially impacted products has been conducted. We are not aware of any impact to our products or systems.</p>\n<p><span class=\"futura-bold\">Further information can be found here:</span><br>\n<a href=\"https://us-cert.cisa.gov/ics/alerts/ics-alert-20-063-01\">https://us-cert.cisa.gov/ics/alerts/ics-alert-20-063-01</a></p>\n<p>If further analysis identifies impacted product, we will communicate through our normal customer communications methods directly from the applicable Stryker division.</p>\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Jul 22 2020 17:59:48 GMT+0000",
